From 9f52840a118f3423b3b86ac9a15ac45a0e2fbc0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:42:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: Dolby Vision in IPT-PQ-c2, as licensed
 players send it

Licensed players are reported to send TV-led Dolby Vision in IPT-PQ-c2
whatever the profile: the TV-led output mode of Amlogic's licensed driver
is "IPT tunnel" for every source, YBLOD reports IPT matrices in captures of
two licensed Amlogic players with profile 8.1, and a published comparison
(DMDreview) reports IPT from a MediaTek Blu-ray player and two Amlogic
players with profile 7 FEL. The bridge sent the composer's YCbCr for
profiles 7 and 8, which clause 6 of ETSI GS CCM 001 allows; a TV then
converts it itself, and between the pairs of 4:2:2 chroma the intensity it
computes depends on how it interpolates the chroma (on a software renderer,
with linear interpolation: up to 9 to 120 codes of 4096 on pictures of a
profile 7 stream, 301 at hard colour edges; with an IPT tunnel, 3 at most).

New: pass 9 of the source packer converts the composer's YCbCr picture to
IPT-PQ-c2 in floats after its chroma rows are made (and after a scaled
picture is scaled): the chroma of every pixel (between the pairs, the same
Lanczos 6 in integers as the rows), YCCtoRGB of the RPU, the PQ EOTF, the
LMS of BT.2020 without the crosstalk of profile 5, the PQ OETF and the
inverse of YCCtoRGB of profile 5; I of every pixel, P and T of each pair
from its even pixel. The passes after it take its luma and rows with the
parameters that dvbridge_source_setup() makes for an RPU of profile 5, so
the picture that Kodi draws over, the GUI's pixels converted back (pass 8)
and the transport work as for profile 5. The DM header carries the matrices
of the RPUs of profile 5 (dvbridge_ipt.h) and signal_color_space 2. Only a
YCbCr picture with the RGBtoLMS of BT.2020; profile 5, the converted
transport and every other path are as they were.

dvbridge_render_use_ipt() asks for it (off by default; Kodi turns it on).
At fidelity step-down level 3 the composer's YCbCr goes out instead: it
saves the conversion of every pixel and comes last, as its change between
the pairs is the largest (dvbridge_render_step_levels(): 0xf with the
residual, 0x9 without, for such pictures).

Measured on a software renderer (zink on lavapipe), 14 pictures of a
profile 7 FEL stream: the tunnel is the conversion in double precision but
for 1 code in 0.6 % of the I samples, 3.6 % of P and 1.0 % of T (float
arithmetic); the DM header is IPT with the profile 5 matrices; the direct
and the composed ways give the same bytes; pixels without a GUI over them
are the direct way's; a scaled picture is within 0.22 Delta E ITP of its
YCbCr tunnel; with the conversion off, every byte as before, and profile 5
the same bytes with it on and off. Two mutations of the bridge (a
coefficient of the matrix, Cb and Cr swapped) are caught. A 4K frame takes
58 ms more there (99 to 157 ms); on a GPU, not measured.
